- `Shift` + arrow keys — select text on the command line; type or paste to replace the selection
- `Cmd+A` select all, `Cmd+C` copy, `Cmd+X` cut, `Cmd+Z` undo, `Cmd+Shift+Z` redo
- Paste with your terminal's own paste shortcut; it replaces a selection
- Run `edit-select config` to change the mouse behaviour and the key bindings
- Needs terminal key bindings that send these sequences to the shell (examples for Ghostty, iTerm2, Kitty, WezTerm and VS Code are in the plugin's README); restart the terminal afterwards
- Mouse selections need Accessibility permission for your terminal: run `edit-select setup-ax`
- A manual install of the plugin blocks this module: remove its `source` line from `~/.zshrc`, delete the old clone and stop its agent, otherwise nothing is loaded from here
